---
layout: layouts/page.njk
---
<h1 class="sr-only">Work&amp;Stay Korea</h1>

{#
  Region-info shell (architecture.md §3): one shared region-card.njk partial feeds two
  render modes, switched by a width-only CSS breakpoint (768px) — never both at once, never
  recomputed on resize.
    - Wide (region-infographic): all 6 regions permanently visible around the map, in two
      fixed-position columns connected to the map by static, hand-positioned SVG leader lines.
      Cross-hover (card <-> map region <-> leader line, Phase 18) is pure CSS (:has()), no JS —
      each card/line carries a matching data-slug/data-region-slug for the selectors to key off.
    - Narrow (region-single): the map alone, full width, followed by one static card in normal
      flow. Tap-to-fill-this-card-from-the-map is real behavior deferred to a later phase
      (korea-map.js/region-card.js are still stub init()s) — this card shows Gyeonggi-do as the
      default so the DOM/CSS structure and mock data wiring are provable now.
  Left/right column assignment follows each region's actual west/east position on the map
  (verified against live centroid measurement, not eyeballed — Korea's landmass genuinely
  splits 4-west/2-east, not 3/3: Gyeonggi/Chungcheong/Jeolla/Jeju all sit west of the map's own
  center line, only Gangwon/Gyeongsang sit east), ordered top-to-bottom (N to S) within each
  column — see leader-line coordinates below, which target each region's actual centroid on the
  map (not the map's outer edge) so the lines visually connect to the region itself.
#}
<section id="map" class="region-infographic" aria-label="Region overview">
  <div class="region-infographic__col region-infographic__col--left">
    {% for slug in ["gyeonggi-do", "chungcheong-do", "jeolla-do", "jeju-do"] %}
    {% set region = regions | findBySlug(slug) %}
    {% set cost = costOfLiving | findBySlug(slug) %}
    {% set modifier = "infographic" %}
    {% include "partials/region-card.njk" %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  {% include "partials/korea-map.njk" %}

  <div class="region-infographic__col region-infographic__col--right">
    {% for slug in ["gangwon-do", "gyeongsang-do"] %}
    {% set region = regions | findBySlug(slug) %}
    {% set cost = costOfLiving | findBySlug(slug) %}
    {% set modifier = "infographic" %}
    {% include "partials/region-card.njk" %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <svg class="region-infographic__lines" viewBox="0 0 880 950" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <line data-slug="gyeonggi-do" x1="210" y1="221.2" x2="358.8" y2="193.5" />
    <line data-slug="chungcheong-do" x1="210" y1="390.4" x2="377.9" y2="352.6" />
    <line data-slug="jeolla-do" x1="210" y1="559.6" x2="344.5" y2="587.3" />
    <line data-slug="jeju-do" x1="210" y1="728.8" x2="285.9" y2="911.3" />
    <line data-slug="gangwon-do" x1="670" y1="390.4" x2="489.6" y2="160.2" />
    <line data-slug="gyeongsang-do" x1="670" y1="559.6" x2="529.9" y2="462.3" />
  </svg>
</section>

<section class="region-single" aria-label="Selected region">
  {% set region = regions | findBySlug("gyeonggi-do") %}
  {% set cost = costOfLiving | findBySlug("gyeonggi-do") %}
  {% set modifier = "single" %}
  {% include "partials/region-card.njk" %}
</section>
